<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom half yr profit rises 6.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Telecom half yr profit rises 6.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30</p>
<p>				 (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				 360.9 vs 338.0</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 19.1 vs 17.9</p>
<p>    Half yr div (cents)			 19 vs 17</p>
<p>    Second qtr div (cents)		   9.5 vs 8.5</p>
<p>    Turnover (billion)			1.66 vs 1.53</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			    541.4 vs 506.1</p>
<p>    Tax					  180.5 vs 167.4</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (billion)	  1.89 vs same</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credit.  </p>
<p>Pay date Dec 16 New Zealand and Australia, Dec 23 U.S</p>
<p>Reg date Dec 6</p>
<p>Note - Telecom Corp of New Zealand is a telephone utility owned 24.8 percent by Ameritech Corp and 24.8 percent by Bell Atlantic Corp. Analysts had forecast net profit at between $360-375 million.</p>
<p>Balance sheet (in billions unless stated)</p>
<p>    Current assets			    0.80 vs 0.76</p>
<p>    Total assets				4.62 vs 4.53</p>
<p>    Current liabilities		     1.10 vs 1.38</p>
<p>    Total liabilities			 2.47 vs 2.42</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity		    2.15 vs 2.10</p>
<p>    Cashflow from operating activities  0.67 vs 0.58</p>
<p>    Cashflow from investing activities(0.27) vs (0.24)</p>
<p>	  -- Wellington newsroom 64 4 473-4746</p>
</text>
